      content:
          'A 45-year-old male is admitted to the acute rehabilitation unit 3 weeks after orthotopic heart transplant for end-stage non-ischemic dilated cardiomyopathy. He had been listed as Status 4 on the transplant waitlist for 14 months, during which he was supported with a left ventricular assist device (LVAD) as bridge to transplant. His post-transplant course was complicated by acute cellular rejection (Grade 2R) treated with pulse methylprednisolone on post-operative day 10, now resolved on surveillance biopsy. He is profoundly deconditioned — unable to stand for more than 2 minutes, requires moderate assist for transfers, and becomes dyspneic walking 30 feet. He was previously an avid competitive cyclist who completed century rides (100 miles), and his primary question to the rehab team is: "When can I race again?"',
