      content:
          '**Vitals**: BP 132/78 mmHg, HR 98 bpm (resting — note: denervated heart), RR 18, SpO2 97% on RA, Temp 36.7C, Weight 78 kg, BMI 25.5.\n\n**Cardiovascular**:\n- **Resting HR**: 98 bpm — elevated baseline consistent with denervated donor heart (loss of vagal tone). Regular rhythm.\n- **Heart sounds**: Normal S1/S2, no murmurs, no S3/S4.\n- **Sternotomy incision**: Well-healed, stable, no drainage or erythema.\n- **JVP**: Not elevated. No peripheral edema.\n\n**Pulmonary**: Clear to auscultation bilaterally. No pleural effusion on recent CXR. Mild dyspnea with sustained conversation.\n\n**Musculoskeletal**:\n- **Proximal weakness**: Hip flexors 3+/5 bilaterally, knee extensors 4-/5 bilaterally, shoulder flexors 4/5 bilaterally. Distal strength 4+/5 throughout.\n- **Muscle atrophy**: Visible quadriceps and gluteal wasting. Reduced calf circumference bilaterally.\n- **ROM**: Full throughout. Sternal precautions in effect.\n- **Grip strength**: R 28 kg, L 26 kg (reduced from estimated baseline of 45+ kg).\n\n**Neurologic**: Alert, oriented. Fine tremor bilateral hands (tacrolimus). Sensation intact. Reflexes 2+ and symmetric. No focal deficits.\n\n**Skin**: Sternotomy scar healing well. LVAD driveline exit site (left abdomen) — healing, no infection signs. Multiple ecchymoses on arms (anticoagulation/steroid-related).\n\n**Functional Testing**:\n- **6-Minute Walk Test**: 125 meters (predicted >550 meters for age — severely deconditioned)\n- **30-second chair stand**: 3 repetitions with armrest use (severely impaired)\n- **Modified Borg Dyspnea Scale**: 5/10 after 6MWT\n- **Heart rate response during 6MWT**: Resting 98 bpm, peak 108 bpm (blunted chronotropic response — denervated heart)',
